es-Lakşmaņa and Sugriva, spoke respectfully the following words fraught with propriety.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.821,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-19-31"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6013019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e3db97fe173b8f5dacf49dfede75cd4a146570cbed63b31352417c8a409f073d","compact":"3150f2b5f9e365d65b4fce14be0fe3542602f3b68b693492123b1050976c4821","nasal":"3150f2b5f9e365d65b4fce14be0fe3542602f3b68b693492123b1050976c4821"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-13-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":13,"verse":20,"english":"Why shall not the well-meaning words of Vibhīşaņa expressed now, please us O Rāghava, O you best of men?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.867,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-19-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6013020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"68812a20e6b1ed711e75061842315473f5737fa409cdf216a854ed597793188e","compact":"620b2322af14183be9d55d25fda1c6194764dbeb2733205b55dc4c85f12303d5","nasal":"620b2322af14183be9d55d25fda1c6194764dbeb2733205b55dc4c85f12303d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-13-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":13,"verse":21,"english":"Without constructing a bridge over the deep, the terrible abode of Varuņa, even the celestials and their lord (India) cannot get at the city of Lanka.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.779,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-19-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6013021","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b39b44c91befd22dcbf8f4870abf4be8692c6944b3924d95cff59c846851e7de","compact":"d56c7c07a917387519e3a98f363f49a15b1eaf099eb29443659400f7a8e42ef3","nasal":"e4e74f1269817340ec7e139b30a0c55fbc7e7446fc59c8763f703ac37c28e060"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-13-22","kand